Eli: FYI opened PR to standardize naming across docs + SDKs: replace `quota` -> `quota_limits` and add a sample "per-tier" panel for the usage dashboard. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4892

Nina: Nice. Can you include a short migration snippet showing header + response shape? Folks keep hitting mismatch when reading `X-Quota` vs new body fields.

Eli: Adding both. Minimal response shape example I'll put in the migration guide: 

```json
{
  "tenant": "acct_987",
  "quota_limits": {
    "base": 100000,
    "burst": 25000,
    "grace": -5000,
    "effective": 120000
  },
  "used": 95000
}
```

Jorge: Can you show a quick JS SDK snippet that reads effective and computes percent used? That's what our customers search for.

Eli: Sure — adding node example: 

```javascript
// JS v2 SDK example
import Redwood from 'redwood-sdk';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
async function check() {
  const resp = await client.v2.usage.getQuotaLimits({ tenant: 'acct_987' });
  const eff = resp.quota_limits.effective;
  const used = resp.used;
  console.log(`used: ${used}/${eff} (${(used/eff*100).toFixed(1)}%)`);
}
check();
```

Nina: Also include curl + python examples in same PR. People still copy-paste curl into monitoring scripts.

Eli: Will do. Side note: adding recommended alert rule text to the panel section: `sum(increase(usage_tokens_total[5m])) by (tier) / quota_limits_effective > 0.85 for 10m`. Add guidance about burst depletion causing transient spikes.

Jorge: Add a tiny mapping table in the migration doc showing old header -> new field: `X-Quota-Remaining` -> `quota_limits.effective - used`, and show numeric example per tenant.

BuildBot: CI started for branch docs/pr/4892. Link check and markdown lint scheduled.

DocsBot: link-checker: found 2 issues -> broken internal anchor `#old-quota-headers` and legacy example image link `docs/images/quota-graph.png` 404. Suggest updating anchor to `#legacy-header-mapping` and replacing image with `images/quota-graph-v2.png`.

Eli: Thanks. I'll update anchors and swap the image. Nina, can you quick review the python snippet?

Nina: Reviewing now. One nit: use `client.v2` naming consistently; earlier PR accidentally used `client()` factory which is ambiguous. Also mention compatibility shim exists for 1 release.

Eli: Good catch. I'll add a short note under migration: "Compatibility: SDK provides shim mapping `quota` -> `quota_limits` for one release; remove shim after deprecation window."

Jorge: For the dashboard JSON, can you paste an import blob so Eng-SRE can quickly import and tweak legend colors? We should include `tier` label by default.

Eli: Dropping the minimal panel JSON in the PR description (time-series with tier grouping). Also added suggested alert expressions + alert runbook link.

